<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42446" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρῑθ-εύομαι</span></b> , Dep., (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔριθος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>serve, work for hire,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>To.</u>
				2.11
			</span></i>:—so in 
				Act.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				1.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of public
			officers or characters, <i>canvass, intrigue for office,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἐριθευόμενοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1303a16
				</span></i>
			 ; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξεριθεύομαι.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> later 
				Act.
			, generally, <i>compete with,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span> Sch.<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				833
			</span></i> : abs., <i>indulge in petty intrigue,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1162.23
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
